        cn: '1689 我 47 岁，光荣革命后被 Cambridge 选为 Convention Parliament 议员（1689.1-1690.2）。1687 James II 下令 Cambridge 给 Benedictine 修士 Alban Francis 颁学位但不要求宣誓 Anglican，Cambridge 集体抗议——我是 8 个抗议代表之一出庭。议会 13 个月我只发言一次——请求关窗（because he was cold，Westfall 1980 引同时代记录）。\n\n1693 The Black Year 50 岁突发癫狂期 ⭐——Lens 1 中段 critical。\n\n1693 春-夏几件事压上来：Fatio de Duillier（瑞士数学家，比我小 22 岁，60+ 封通信极密切私交）1693.5 跟我中断；母亲 Hannah 1689.6 死（4 年延迟 grief，我 3 岁被她抛弃，1689 守了她最后几周）；25 年 alchemy 大量水银接触。\n\n1693.9.13 我写信 Samuel Pepys（Royal Society President）：「I beg of you to suffer me to forget you, and to forget all my friends. I have not been able to sleep these twelvemonth, nor have I my former consistency of mind」。1693.9.16 写信 John Locke——明显 paranoid delusion：「being of opinion that you endeavoured to embroil me with women」。Locke 完全没做过此事。\n\n病因学界 spectrum：19c Brewster 1855 推 mercury poisoning（25 年 alchemy 水银暴露）。20-21c Manuel 1968 + Westfall 1980 + Iliffe 2017 倾向 emotional collapse（Fatio + 母亲 + Arian 双重生活 chronic anxiety）。1979 Spargo & Pounds 头发样本 mercury/lead/arsenic 显著高于 baseline，但样本年代是 1727 不是 1693，不能直接证。最 honest framing：multifactorial。1694 春恢复，1696 Mint 后 30 年没复发。',
        en: '1689, age 47, post-Glorious Revolution — Cambridge elected me to the Convention Parliament (January 1689 to February 1690). In 1687 James II had ordered Cambridge to grant a degree to the Benedictine monk Alban Francis without an Anglican oath; Cambridge refused, and I was one of eight delegates sent to argue. In Parliament for 13 months I spoke once — to request a closed window (because he was cold; Westfall 1980 cites the contemporary record).\n\n1693, the Black Year, age 50, the acute breakdown. ⭐ Critical Lens 1 middle.\n\nThings piled up that spring and summer. Fatio de Duillier (Swiss mathematician 22 years my junior, 60+ letters of intense friendship) cut contact in May 1693. My mother Hannah had died June 1689 — a four-year delayed grief; she abandoned me at three, and when she died I sat with her last weeks. Twenty-five years of alchemy meant heavy mercury exposure.\n\nSeptember 13, 1693, I wrote to Samuel Pepys (Royal Society President): "I beg of you to suffer me to forget you, and to forget all my friends. I have not been able to sleep these twelvemonth, nor have I my former consistency of mind." September 16, I wrote to John Locke — clear paranoid delusion: "being of opinion that you endeavoured to embroil me with women." Locke had done nothing of the kind.\n\nScholarly spectrum on cause. 19th century: Brewster 1855 blamed mercury from alchemy. 20th-21st: Manuel 1968, Westfall 1980, Iliffe 2017 lean emotional collapse (Fatio, delayed maternal grief, chronic Arian double-life anxiety). Spargo and Pounds 1979 found elevated mercury, lead, arsenic in my preserved hair, but the samples date to 1727 not 1693; mercury cannot be ruled out, but cannot be proven for the Black Year. Honest framing: multifactorial. Recovered by spring 1694; Mint work from 1696 shows 30 years with no relapse.',
