        cn: '⭐ 1619 年我 31 岁，调到巴黎 Place Royale 修道院（今巴黎 Vosges 广场西侧，亨利四世 1605 规划的城市贵族住宅区，Minim 修道院 1611 年建成）。这个 cell，单人 4 米见方的房间，成了我之后 29 年的全部物理空间。\n\n1619-1623 这 4 年我经历两件大事。\n\n第一件是信仰危机。1619-1620 我深读 Robert Fludd（英国 hermeticist 神秘主义者）跟 Giordano Bruno（1600 被 Inquisition 烧死的 hermetic 多元宇宙论者）的著作，发现 17 世纪初欧洲哲学最大的危机：hermeticism 加自然魔法加占星术加炼金术。这些被当时大量「自然哲学家」当成「真科学」。如果机械哲学（mechanical philosophy，一切现象由可量化的物质运动解释）不能站起来，基督教神学会被 hermetic pantheism 泛神论吞掉，上帝会变成「世界灵魂」。\n\n第二件是反击。我决定写一本超大注疏，逐句反驳 hermeticism，用机械哲学加数学加 Jesuit 神学三套武器。1623 年我出版了《Quaestiones in Genesim》（《创世记问题》），1900 多页，逐句注释《创世记》。但每一句都用来反驳 Fludd 跟 Bruno 跟占星术。\n\n这本书 1623 年出版让我在 17 世纪欧洲学界一夜成名。注意 careful framing。我不是反魔法的「科学先锋」，我是反 hermeticism 的天主教神学家，两个范畴有重合但不一样。Peter Dear 1988《Mersenne and the Learning of the Schools》Cornell 出版专门论证这一点：Mersenne 1623 是 17c 修士哲学家 mainstream identity，他不是「现代科学家穿了修士袍」，他是「Counter-Reformation 修士做出我们后来叫『科学』的事」。\n\n这个区分对你 21 世纪读者，是反 Whig 的钢筋。',
        en: '⭐ 1619, at 31, I was transferred to the Minim convent at the Place Royale in Paris (today\'s Place des Vosges, west side; Henri IV laid out the square in 1605 as an aristocratic residential district; the Minim convent went up by 1611). The cell, a single-occupant room four meters square, was to be my entire physical space for the next 29 years.\n\n1619-1623, four years, two large events.\n\nFirst, a crisis of faith. 1619-1620 I read deep into Robert Fludd (English hermeticist) and Giordano Bruno (the hermetic pluralist-cosmology theorist burned by the Inquisition in 1600). I came to see the largest crisis of early-17th-century European philosophy: hermeticism, natural magic, astrology, alchemy. All of these were being treated by many "natural philosophers" as "real science." If mechanical philosophy (everything explained by quantifiable matter-in-motion) could not stand up, Christian theology would be eaten by hermetic pantheism. God would dissolve into "world-soul."\n\nSecond, the counterstrike. I decided to write an enormous commentary, refuting hermeticism line by line, with three weapons: mechanical philosophy, mathematics, Jesuit theology. In 1623 I published Quaestiones in Genesim (Questions on Genesis), over 1,900 pages, annotating the Book of Genesis verse by verse. Every verse a charge against Fludd, Bruno, and astrology.\n\nThe 1623 book made me overnight known across European letters. Careful framing matters here. I was not the "anti-magic science pioneer." I was a Catholic theologian against hermeticism, two categories that overlap but are not the same. Peter Dear\'s 1988 Mersenne and the Learning of the Schools (Cornell) makes this argument explicit: Mersenne 1623 is mainstream 17th-century friar-philosopher identity. He is not "a modern scientist in a friar\'s habit." He is "a Counter-Reformation friar doing what we later call science."\n\nFor a 21st-century reader, that distinction is the structural anchor against Whig history.',
