      content: {
        cn: '1623-1648 这 25 年，我 35 到 60 岁，做了一件 17 世纪没人做过的事。\n\n我的 Place Royale cell 变成欧洲自然哲学的邮政交换台。Cornelis de Waard 1932-1988 编了 17 卷《Correspondance du P. Marin Mersenne》，大约 3000 封信，是我现存的通信总量（活着时实际写过的应该更多，很多丢失）。\n\n核心通信圈，史学家有出入。Peter Dear 1988 比较窄的定义大约 60-70 人，其他人估到 100。中间数 60-100。这个数字 careful framing：我不是给所有人写，是给一个有规模的 inner circle。\n\n4 个最有故事的人，每人一句他们当时在做什么 + 我寄给他们什么。\n\nGalileo 在 Florence Arcetri 软禁中写《Discorsi》力学手稿，我 1633-1638 帮他走私出版。Descartes 在 Holland Egmond 隐居写《Meditationes》，1640 寄我手稿求 6 组反对者 reply。Pascal 1644 春 20 岁在 Paris 父亲家，我亲手把 Torricelli 真空数据讲给他。Hobbes 1640 流亡 Paris 逃英国内战，我寄他 Descartes 手稿请他写 Third Objections（唯物论攻击）。\n\n剩下 8 个核心 hub 合并一句: Toulouse 的 Fermat（费马，地方法官 + 业余数学家）、Provence 的 Gassendi（伽桑狄，神父 + 原子论复兴者）、Paris 的 Roberval、Holland 的 Beeckman、Hague 的 Constantijn Huygens、Aix 的 Peiresc、英国的 Haak、London 的 Hartlib——8 个 hub 各自再延伸出几十人，我的 inner circle 就是这样滚出去的。\n\n你看这张地图。巴黎、Florence、Holland、Toulouse、Provence、Hague、Aix、London。半个西欧。我没出过 Paris，但我让 Paris 成为这个网的中心。我用的工具：羽毛笔加信纸加邮政马车（17 世纪欧洲邮政，Paris 到 Florence 走 3 周，Paris 到 Hague 走 6 天）。\n\ncross-Topic 钩子: 同一时期 Jesuit Matteo Ricci 利玛窦（1552-1610）在北京 1601-1610 当 Wanli 皇帝技术顾问，1607 年跟徐光启（1562-1633）合译 Euclid《几何原本》(Elements) 前 6 卷——这是中国第一次接触欧氏几何。我 1611 加入 Minim 修会的同年（利玛窦 1610 刚死），中国跟欧洲的 Jesuit 知识交换网比我的 Paris 通信网早 10-20 年。\n\n25 年我没结过婚（修士不能），没出过国，只在 cell 里写信。我把欧洲自然哲学连了起来。',
        en: '1623-1648, 25 years, ages 35 to 60, I did what nobody in the 17th century had done.\n\nMy Place Royale cell became the postal switchboard of European natural philosophy. Cornelis de Waard\'s Correspondance du P. Marin Mersenne (17 volumes, 1932-1988) gathers around 3,000 surviving letters, the total of my correspondence. The actual lifetime number was higher; much was lost.\n\nThe core circle, historians disagree on size. Peter Dear\'s 1988 narrow definition: about 60-70. Others count 100. The midpoint is 60-100. Careful framing: I did not write to everyone equally. I had a sized inner circle.\n\nThe four with the strongest stories — each one in a sentence: what they were doing, what I sent them.\n\nGalileo, in Florence under house arrest at Arcetri, was writing the Discorsi mechanics manuscript — I organized its 1633-1638 smuggling out. Descartes, in seclusion in Holland at Egmond writing the Meditationes, sent me the 1640 manuscript and asked me to gather six sets of Objections. Pascal, twenty in spring 1644 at his father\'s house in Paris — I went there myself and laid Torricelli\'s vacuum data in front of him. Hobbes, in exile in Paris from 1640 fleeing the English Civil War — I sent him Descartes\'s manuscript and asked him for the Third Objections (the materialist critique).\n\nThe remaining eight hubs in one sentence: Fermat in Toulouse (provincial magistrate and amateur mathematician), Gassendi in Provence (priest, reviver of atomism), Roberval in Paris, Beeckman in Holland, Constantijn Huygens at The Hague, Peiresc in Aix, Haak in England, Hartlib in London — each hub with dozens more behind it, and that is how my inner circle radiated outward.\n\nLook at the map. Paris, Florence, Holland, Toulouse, Provence, The Hague, Aix, London. Half of Western Europe. I never left Paris. I made Paris the center. The instruments: a quill, paper, the postal carriage. (17th-century postal speed: Paris to Florence about three weeks; Paris to The Hague about six days.)\n\nCross-Topic hook: in the same period the Jesuit Matteo Ricci (1552-1610) lived in Beijing from 1601 to 1610 as a technical adviser to the Wanli emperor; in 1607 he and Xu Guangqi (1562-1633) co-translated the first six books of Euclid\'s Elements — China\'s first encounter with Euclidean geometry. The year I entered the Minim Order, 1611 (just after Ricci\'s death in 1610), the Jesuit knowledge-exchange network between China and Europe was already running, predating my Paris correspondence by ten to twenty years.\n\nFor 25 years I never married (a friar cannot), never left the country, only wrote letters in a cell. I stitched European natural philosophy together.',
      },
      deliverGoal: 'N4 1623-48 25 年 letter-broker — de Waard 17 卷 ~3000 封信 + 60-100 人核心圈 careful framing (Peter Dear 1988 60-70, 其他 100) + 12 通信对象地图 (Galileo Florence, Descartes Holland, Pascal Paris, Hobbes Paris, Fermat Toulouse, Gassendi Provence, Roberval Paris, Beeckman Holland, Huygens Hague, Peiresc Aix, Haak England, Hartlib London) + Paris-Florence 3 周 + Paris-Hague 6 天 + 没出过 Paris 但把 Paris 变中央',
      engagementHook: '我没出过 Paris，25 年，羽毛笔加信纸加邮政马车。但我把欧洲自然哲学连了起来。一个不动的 broker 撬动 8000 公里的网。你怎么读「静止 hub vs 流动 nodes」？',
