      id: 'maria-n7',
      type: 'narrative',
      content: {
        cn: '1710 年 7 月 25 日——Gottfried 死了——71 岁。\n\n我 40 岁守寡。\n\n3 个月后——1710 年 10 月——我正式申请接任 Berlin Academy astronomer 职位。\n\n我的 case 强:\n- 18 年观测经验（1692-1710）\n- 1702 彗星发现（Leibniz 已私下确认是我）\n- 已在 Berlin Academy 观测台日常工作 8 年（1702-1710 半数观测我做）\n- 知道所有 instruments / 数据 / calendar 编制流程\n\nLeibniz 作为 Academy President 强力支持。Leibniz 1710 年 10 月 18 日给 Berlin Academy Council 的信原文（Schiebinger 1989, p. 95）:\n\n「Frau Kirch is one of the most learned astronomers now living. She has performed services to the Academy that no man in our employ could have done better. To dismiss her now would be a great injustice and a great loss.」\n\n（Frau Kirch 女士是当今活着的最博学的天文学家之一。她为 Academy 做的工作，我们雇的任何男人都做不到更好。现在赶她走是巨大的不公也是巨大的损失。）\n\nLeibniz 是 Newton 的微积分对手，是 Mersenne 网络的「孙辈」，1700 年自己创办的 Academy。他自己赌上声誉支持我。\n\n但 1711 年 1 月 18 日 Berlin Academy Council 否决了 Leibniz 自己。\n\n据 Schiebinger 1989 转述（p. 96），Council 拒绝我的大意是：让一个 Frauenzimmer 当 astronomer 会给 Academy 开一个不光彩的先例。（这是对史料大意的转述，不是逐字 archive 原文——权威来源里 surface 出来的措辞并不一致，秘书 Jablonski 的说法是「留用她会让旁人更瞠目」、Council 的理由记为「怕开先例」。）\n\ninline gloss: Frauenzimmer 是 17-18c 德语，字面意思「女性的房间」（women\'s apartments）。用「房间」代指「女性」是当时德语 standard idiom，暗含「女性应留私人空间，不应公开露面」的 patriarchal 假设。Council 用这个词不是 neutral，是带 semantic loading 的。\n\n你 21 世纪 7 年级听清楚: 我不是因为「不够 qualified」被拒，Leibniz 已认证。真实理由是: 一旦我任职，Academy 就开了「女性可任职」先例，未来无法关门。Council 怕这个 institutional precedent。\n\n这里有一根 cross-lens 钩子。同一年 1710——Cambridge 用「Arian 异端」开除 William Whiston（Newton 的 protégé，接 Newton Lucasian Chair 的人）。两个 institution 用不同理由开除两种不可见信仰（女性身份 / 异端神学）——但同一种 logic「我们怕开先例」。\n\nIliffe 2017《Priest of Nature》(Oxford) 把这两件事放进同一个 institutional 自我保护框架。1710-1712 是新生科学机构最 sharp 的「关门」时刻。',
        en: 'On 25 July 1710 Gottfried died, at 71.\n\nI was 40, a widow.\n\nThree months later, in October 1710, I formally applied to succeed him as Berlin Academy astronomer.\n\nMy case was strong:\n- 18 years of observation (1692-1710)\n- the 1702 comet (Leibniz had already privately confirmed it was mine)\n- 8 years already inside the Berlin Academy observatory, doing roughly half the observations from 1702 to 1710\n- mastery of every instrument, dataset, and step of the calendar pipeline\n\nLeibniz, as Academy president, threw his weight behind me. His 18 October 1710 letter to the Berlin Academy Council (Schiebinger 1989, p. 95):\n\n"Frau Kirch is one of the most learned astronomers now living. She has performed services to the Academy that no man in our employ could have done better. To dismiss her now would be a great injustice and a great loss."\n\nLeibniz — Newton\'s rival in the calculus dispute, "grandchild" of Mersenne\'s network, founder of the Academy in 1700 — staked his own reputation on me.\n\nOn 18 January 1711 the Berlin Academy Council overruled Leibniz himself.\n\nAs Schiebinger 1989 (p. 96) reports it, the gist of the Council\'s refusal was that employing a Frauenzimmer as astronomer would set an unflattering precedent for the Academy. (This is a paraphrase of the gist, not a verbatim archive original — the surviving sources do not agree on the exact wording: the secretary Jablonski warned that keeping her on would make "mouths gape even wider," and the Council\'s stated reason is recorded as fear of setting a precedent.)\n\nInline gloss: Frauenzimmer — 17th-18th-century German — literally "women\'s apartments." Using "the rooms" to stand for "women" was standard idiom of the day, carrying the patriarchal assumption that women belonged in private spaces and should not appear in public. The Council\'s choice of word was not neutral — it was semantically loaded.\n\n21st-century 7th grade hear this clearly: I was not refused for lack of qualifications. Leibniz had certified me. The real reason was that the moment I was appointed, the Academy would have set a "women may hold posts" precedent — a door it could not later close. The Council feared the institutional precedent.\n\nA cross-lens hook: in the same year, 1710, Cambridge expelled William Whiston (Newton\'s protégé, his successor in the Lucasian Chair) on charges of Arian heresy. Two institutions, two different official reasons, two different invisible affiliations (gender, theological heresy) — but the same logic: "we fear the precedent."\n\nIliffe 2017, Priest of Nature (Oxford), places both events inside one frame of institutional self-protection. 1710-1712 is the sharpest "closing the door" moment in the new scientific institutions.',
      },
      deliverGoal: 'N7 1710.7.25 Gottfried 死 71 岁 / Maria 40 岁守寡 / 1710.10 申请接任 Berlin Academy astronomer / 18 年经验 + 1702 彗星 + 8 年日常工作 + 知道所有流程 / Leibniz 1710.10.18 信原文「one of the most learned astronomers now living」/ 1711.1.18 Council 否决: 据 Schiebinger 1989 转述大意「让一个 Frauenzimmer 当 astronomer 会给 Academy 开不光彩先例」(转述非逐字 archive 原文; 权威措辞不一: Jablonski「旁人会更瞠目」/「怕开先例」) / Frauenzimmer inline gloss 17-18c 德语 patriarchal semantic loading / 真实理由「institutional precedent fear」/ ⭐ cross-lens 钩 1710 Cambridge 开除 Whiston (Newton protégé) Arian 异端 同 institutional 自我保护 (Iliffe 2017)',
      engagementHook: '「我们怕开先例」——你 21 世纪有没有过这种「他们不是反对你这个人——是怕你后面带来的人」的感觉？',
